  "notes": [
    "ADR 0009 \u00a7Consequences fixture. The file-level version of `mcp-nondeterministic-response`, and cheaper.",
    "Two fs.read events for /repo/notes.md inside one computation with different hashes. The store already recorded this as a conflict; before W9.1 the engine surfaced it only as a `graph.edge_conflict` diagnostic, because no reason code existed \u2014 so the conflict was visible in the log while the certificate still said `valid`.",
    "`unknown`, not `stale`: nothing observed drift against the recorded fingerprint. What is missing is knowledge of WHICH observation the computation consumed, and absence of that is unknown (invariant #7).",
    "The edge verdict is forced regardless of what a probe says. A probe confirming the recorded fingerprint still matches proves nothing about the other observation, so `input_probes` is deliberately retained from file-dep to show the forcing is not an artefact of having no probe."
  ],
